Z||000000||KnightRyder31||04-30-2000||04:14 PM||||How do I adjust my Idle? I want to increase my 84 Fiero 2M4's idle by about 500RPM. When I'm in park, its just fine, but when I'm stoped at a red light, the idle dropes to about 500RPM. When it does this, it makes my whole car viberate hard. I tried to get at the screw that adjusts the RPM, but I cant get at it. Please help, my step-father works for GM and cant even figure it out.<BR>----Knight----||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||04-30-2000||04:38 PM||||First thing I always check is the base timing, because that's one thing that directly affects the idle.... Before you really mess with that, make sure you get a shop manual.  The Fiero's require a special procedure to check and adjust timing, and I would trust Joe-blo mechanic to do it correctly.  I think there's also an idle adjustment screw on the TBI somewhere but I'm a V6 guy... sorry||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||04-30-2000||05:00 PM||||You should not adjust the idle on electronic fuel injected cars, it will mess them up, or so I've been told. Something is wrong, you need to pull the ECM trouble codes and see what that tells you. Undoubtedly, a sensor is screwing up or something is wrong. Normally, the ECM (computer) adjusts the idle automatically, but is apparently getting a bad signal.||||reg||1
